    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset for a GWAS cohort of 17,913 samples and 4,070,585 variants, reporting total and per-chromosome file sizes.",
    "rationale": "Standard PLINK binary .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the largest chromosome's variant count (313,418). Per-chromosome file count = 25 for a human GWAS (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), consistent with the largest chromosome carrying 313,418 variants (chr1).",
